<plain>
<text x="50.8" y="3.81" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">W1  USB-C cable (PSU captive), 5.1 V 5 A PD</text>
<text x="-12.7" y="3.81" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">230 V AC mains</text>
<text x="137.16" y="-24.13" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">W2  micro-HDMI (D) -&gt; HDMI (A) cable: video 800x480 + HDMI audio</text>
<text x="134.62" y="-90.17" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">W3  USB-A -&gt; micro-USB DATA cable: touch (USB HID) + screen power ~400 mA</text>
<text x="154.94" y="-123.19" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-right">Headset (V1 sound = HDMI audio)</text>
<text x="279.4" y="3.81" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">W4  FFC 22-pin 0.5 mm 200 mm REVERSE (supplied): DSI + touch I2C + 3V3</text>
<text x="314.96" y="-69.85" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">W5  2-wire lead: red = 5V (pin 4), black = GND (pin 6)</text>
<text x="320.04" y="-128.27" size="1.778" layer="97" align="top-center">! GPIO 5V is not fused: one pin off can kill the Pi. Power off before plugging.</text>
<text x="279.4" y="-138.43" size="1.778" layer="97" align="bottom-center">W6  Fan lead JST-SH 4p (captive)</text>
